!! Real-world example: Automotive safety system requirements

This example models a subset of ISO 26262-style requirements for an autonomous emergency braking (AEB) system. Requirements are categorized by type using `classDef`: functional requirements, performance requirements, and interface requirements. Each requirement element is traced to the software component that satisfies or verifies it.

```
requirementDiagram
    accTitle: AEB system requirements traceability
    accDescr: Requirement types and satisfies/verifies/traces relationships

    %% ── Functional requirements ─────────────────
    functionalRequirement aeb_activate {
        id: AEB-001
        text: The AEB system shall activate braking when TTC < 1.5 s.
        risk: high
        verifymethod: test
    }
    functionalRequirement aeb_override {
        id: AEB-002
        text: The AEB system shall allow driver override at any time.
        risk: high
        verifymethod: inspection
    }

    %% ── Performance requirements ────────────────
    performanceRequirement aeb_latency {
        id: AEB-010
        text: Braking response latency shall not exceed 150 ms from activation.
        risk: medium
        verifymethod: test
    }
    performanceRequirement aeb_sensor_range {
        id: AEB-011
        text: The radar sensor shall detect objects up to 200 m ahead.
        risk: medium
        verifymethod: analysis
    }

    %% ── Interface requirements ──────────────────
    requirement aeb_can_bus {
        id: AEB-020
        text: AEB ECU shall communicate via CAN FD at 5 Mbit/s.
        risk: low
        verifymethod: inspection
    }

    %% ── System elements ─────────────────────────
    element radar_sensor {
        type: hardware
        docRef: HW-SPEC-001
    }
    element aeb_controller {
        type: software
        docRef: SW-SPEC-003
    }
    element brake_actuator {
        type: hardware
        docRef: HW-SPEC-004
    }
    element can_interface {
        type: software
        docRef: SW-SPEC-007
    }

    %% ── Traceability links ───────────────────────
    aeb_controller - satisfies -> aeb_activate
    aeb_controller - satisfies -> aeb_override
    aeb_controller - satisfies -> aeb_latency
    radar_sensor   - satisfies -> aeb_sensor_range
    can_interface  - satisfies -> aeb_can_bus
    aeb_controller - traces   -> aeb_latency
    brake_actuator - refines  -> aeb_activate
```

